This is the README of Server
Server program takes filetered map and the filename in input of callServer method.
It creates a file of given filename with the values from filtered map.
It crates the file in the output directory path, given in config file.

In the CLI command we pass config file as argument.
--config /Users/smritisharma/Workspace/ArcticWolfAssignment/server.conf
server.conf file contains the port number which server listens on and the output directory path to create the file.

To run the program you will need following
1. Maven installed
2. JDK installed

Then run command "mvn clean install" to build the project.
Run the project, this will run the server to listen to clients.